# {{brandName}} database helper ({{osLabel}} {{arch}})

Browsers cannot open raw database connections from an extension. This helper is a small local program that {{brandName}} starts and stops through **native messaging**. A one-time install is required; day-to-day start/stop is automatic.

## What the installer does

1. Copies this `helper/` folder to:

   `{{installDirExample}}`

2. Writes native-messaging manifests for Chrome, Edge, Brave, Chromium, and Firefox (and Windows HKCU registry keys when on Windows).
3. Points the manifest `path` at the installed `{{helperBinary}}` (no Node required).
4. On Windows, copies sibling `detour-pickfile` (native Browse dialog) when present. On macOS, compiles `pickfile-nsopen.scpt` for fast Browse.
5. Changes nothing else on your system.

