## Command line

From this folder (or after install, from the install directory):

```text
{{helperBinary}} install [--extension-id=…] [--no-firefox] [--dry-run] [--brand=detour]
{{helperBinary}} uninstall
{{helperBinary}} doctor
{{helperBinary}} --version
```

With no arguments, the browser spawns the helper for native messaging (stdio JSON-RPC).

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | What to try |
|---------|-------------|
| **Not installed** / Helper missing | Re-run **{{installScript}}**, reload the options page, click **Start** |
| **Native host disconnected** | Run `{{helperBinary}} doctor` and check the binary + manifest paths |
| Moved the `extension/` folder | No action for the helper — the extension id is fixed by the public manifest key |
| Edge or Brave never installed | Installer skips missing browsers; Chrome/Chromium manifests still work |
| Corporate policy blocks native hosts | Ask IT to allow `com.detour.db` (e.g. Chrome `NativeMessagingAllowlist`) |

## Secrets

Passwords and tokens live in your OS keychain (service `com.detour.db`), not in the extension. Uninstall removes manifests and the helper files; clear keychain entries separately if you want secrets gone too.

## Developers

From a Detour repo checkout with Node 24+:

```sh
corepack pnpm --filter @detour/cli exec node --experimental-strip-types src/cli.ts db install
corepack pnpm --filter @detour/cli exec node --experimental-strip-types src/cli.ts db uninstall
```
